Blind Arbiter
Medium aberration, neutral

Armor Class: 16 (natural armor)
Hit Points: 60 (8d8 + 24)
Speed: 0 ft.

STR	DEX	CON	INT	WIS	CHA
8 (-1)	14 (+2)	16 (+3)	10 (+0)	18 (+4)	12 (+1)
Saving Throws Wis +6, Dex +4
Skills Perception +6, Insight +6
Damage Resistances Necrotic, Psychic
Damage Immunities Poison, Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing from nonmagical attacks
Condition Immunities Blinded, Charmed, Frightened, Poisoned
Senses Blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius), Passive Perception 16
Languages Telepathy 60 ft.

Traits
Unlimited Reactions. The Blind Arbiter can take any number of reactions per round, but only one per trigger.

Aura of Intimidation. Creatures that start their turn within 10 feet of the Arbiter must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or have disadvantage on attack rolls against creatures other than the Arbiter until the start of their next turn.

Eerie Stillness. The Arbiter does not take actions or bonus actions, relying solely on its reactions and legendary actions to interact with its environment and adversaries.

Actions
The Blind Arbiter has no actions.

Reactions
Judgment Slash. When a creature within 5 feet of the Arbiter makes an attack, the Arbiter lashes out with an invisible psychic blade.
Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target.
Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) psychic damage.

Deflecting Glare. When a creature casts a spell within 30 feet of the Arbiter, the Arbiter forces the caster to make a DC 14 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the caster takes 9 (2d6 + 2) psychic damage and loses concentration (if applicable).

Grasp of the Abyss. When a creature moves within 10 feet of the Arbiter, the creature must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or be pulled adjacent to the Arbiter and restrained until the end of its next turn.

Reflective Pain. When the Arbiter takes damage from a melee attack, the attacker must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or take psychic damage equal to half the damage dealt to the Arbiter.

Legendary Actions
The Blind Arbiter can take 1 legendary action per round, choosing from the options below. It regains the ability to do so at the start of its turn.

Misty Step (Costs 1 Action). The Arbiter magically teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can sense within range.
